<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to auction 256,990 bags coffee March 5.</title>
<headline>Brazil to auction 256,990 bags coffee March 5.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's government will auction 256,990 60-kg bags of coffee stocks in its next monthly sale March 5, said an official of Banco do Brasil which is to hold the electronic sale.</p>
<p>Of the total, 82,610 bags will be on offer exclusively to the domestic soluble coffee industry, he said.</p>
<p>Details of the coffee to be put up for auction will be available this afternoon.</p>
<p>The sale, scheduled for 1400 local/1700 GMT, will be the largest in a series of monthly auctions throughout the crop year (July/June).</p>
<p>Monday, members of Brazil's new coffee council agreed on the need to increase auctions which previously had been limited to 200,000 bags.</p>
<p>--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
